Found under k286/k287 (2026-10-31). The apply side waits up to 600 s for NFD to label a freshly joined worker (OCP::Cmd::Apply::Workloads gpu_label_timeout) and, since k286, up to 600 s for an AMD node that just joined (OCP::Cmd::Apply::AMDGPU join_ready_timeout). The reason is Cilium's first BPF compile on a fresh node, about 5.5 min on synapse. `ocp node add --gpu` has its own `gpu_label_timeout` of 300 s in lib/OCP/Cmd/Node/Add.pm for the same NFD wait on the same fresh node, so on a node like synapse it can give up before the apply side would.

Done = node add uses the same budget as the apply side for the NFD label wait, read from one place (not a second literal), and a test pins that node add waits with the fresh-node budget. If 300 s there is deliberate, say why in the code and close this.

